      "body": "12 words on top of the A1 clothes unit. A1 gave you the garments; this unit gives you how they are worn — smart or casual — plus jewellery and the small parts.\nFour of the twelve have no honest picture: fashion, jumper, belt and button. jumper is the British word for the sweater you met at A1.",
      "body_cz": "A1 dalo kusy oblečení, A2 přidává styl a doplňky."
    },
    {
      "title": "You will use these words in",
      "frames": [
        "I wear …",
        "This is a …",
        "I have a …",
        "I need a …",
        "Let's talk about …"
      ],
      "note": "pants is the dangerous one. In American English pants = trousers. In British English pants is underwear — so I like your pants means two very different things.",
      "note_cz": "pants = kalhoty (amer.), ale spodní prádlo (brit.). Brit. kalhoty = trousers."
